    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Social Security checks go up 3.6% in January. So who picks that number?",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 4.82,
        "window": 5.43,
        "fill": 0.888
      },
      {
        "scene": "headline",
        "text": "Nobody does. A formula in the law sets it, and the agency just announced the result.",
        "start": 5.7,
        "seconds": 4.35,
        "window": 4.97,
        "fill": 0.875
      },
      {
        "scene": "source",
        "text": "It follows a price index for wage earners, July to September, against the same months a year before.",
        "start": 10.67,
        "seconds": 5.23,
        "window": 5.83,
        "fill": 0.897
      },
      {
        "scene": "rohan",
        "text": "Okay. But what does that mean for my grandma's check?",
        "start": 16.5,
        "seconds": 2.27,
        "window": 2.77,
        "fill": 0.819
      },
      {
        "scene": "year",
        "text": "Say her checks add up to $24,000 a year. The raise adds $864, for $24,864 in all.",
        "start": 19.27,
        "seconds": 8.5,
        "window": 9.1,
        "fill": 0.934
      },
      {
        "scene": "average",
        "text": "For the average retirement check, the agency puts the raise at about $75 a month.",
        "start": 28.37,
        "seconds": 4.64,
        "window": 5.17,
        "fill": 0.897
      },
      {
        "scene": "lesson",
        "text": "It is not a bonus. It is there so the same check can keep buying the same groceries.",
        "start": 33.53,
        "seconds": 4.37,
        "window": 5.0,
        "fill": 0.874
      },
      {
        "scene": "outro",
        "text": "So, what will your raise cover?",
        "start": 38.53,
        "seconds": 1.18,
        "window": 1.77,
        "fill": 0.667
      }
    ]
  },
